extraction_notes: |
  - Underseas, printed 56-57. The O.C.C. at the centre of the Whale Singer
    society - and note that a Whale Singer need not be a cetacean at all; the
    book opens the class to humans, simvan, dog boys, sea titans, amphibs,
    naut''yll and Lemurians, and says only that most members are cetaceans.
  - ITS UNDERWATER NAVIGATION IS STATED TWICE AND THE TWO READINGS AGREE ON THE
    BASE. The class ability list gives it as "base skill 45% +5% per level"; the
    O.C.C. skill list gives it as "Underwater Navigation (+15%)". The catalog
    row is 30%, and 30 + 15 is 45 - so the two are the same number reached two
    ways, which is a free confirmation that the +15% was read correctly. They
    disagree only on the per-level step, 5% against the catalog''s 4%, and the
    ability''s figure is used because it is the one written for this class.
  - THERE IS NO PER-LEVEL OCEAN GRANT, and that is the book rather than an
    omission. Printed 57 item 11 sends the character to the Pursuit of Magic
    rules instead: ocean spells of any level can be learned or purchased at any
    time regardless of experience level. Only the spellsong ladder is a per-level
    grant.
  - THE DOMESTIC BONUS IS STORED WIDER THAN THE BOOK PRINTS IT. Printed 57 gives
    Domestic: Any with +10% to musical instruments only. A category entry
    carries one bonus for every skill in it, so the choice is between granting
    the category whole with the bonus too wide, or narrowing to one skill and
    losing the rest. The category is kept, on the Dragon Ray precedent.
  - NO `sdc_base` AND NO `mdc_base`, so it needs a `CORE_SDC_BY_CLASS` entry.
    1D6: it is a spell caster with Hand to Hand: Basic and one W.P.
  - PILOT''S `except` NAMES FIVE ROWS FOR THE BOOK''S FOUR WORDS, and every one
    was checked against production first, because an unmatched `except` fails
    OPEN and would silently offer a skill the book forbids. The book bars
    robots, power armour, tanks and spacecraft. `Robots & Power Armor` is one
    catalog row covering the first two; the tank row is `Military: Tanks &
    APCs`, NOT `Tanks & APCs`; and "spacecraft" is three rows - `Space: Small
    Spacecraft`, `Space: Space Fighter` and `Space: Starship`. `Space: Antigrav
    Suit` and `Space: Contragravity Pak` are deliberately left takeable: they
    are worn suits rather than spacecraft.
